# Extension metadata, read by the WebUI's extension catalog. See
# configurator/extensions/catalog.py: every card is built from the apt record,
# and any field omitted here silently falls back to a default (the raw package
# name, category "tool"). dpkg strips the XB- prefix in the built record.
XB-Hifiberry-Extension: yes
XB-Extension-Name: Music Assistant
XB-Extension-Category: player
XB-Extension-Needs-Reboot: no
# Served by hifiberry-webui itself, so it resolves before the extension is
# installed and on a device with no internet access.
#
# This is sendspin's own icon (the same one data/etc/hifiberry/players.d/
# icons/sendspin.svg installs for the Players page), carried by the WebUI
# from 0.21.9 so it resolves before the extension is installed.
#
# The two generic stand-ins tried before both failed, in opposite
# directions: music.svg is drawn on a 115-unit viewBox where the rest of the
# set uses 23, so its strokes came out five times too thin and antialiased to
# grey; music-note-simple-light.svg is a fill-designed silhouette, so with
# fill:none the stroke traced the outline of the outline and read far too
# heavy. Check a candidate is genuine stroke geometry, not a filled shape.
XB-Extension-Icon-Url: /images/svg/sendspin.svg
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
 libasound2 | libasound2t64, libcurl4 | libcurl4t64, libavahi-compat-libdnssd1, hifiberry-configurator (>= 2.17.6)
Description: Sendspin player for HiFiBerryOS
 Renders Music Assistant's native Sendspin stream to the HiFiBerry sound card,
 reports metadata to audiocontrol, and forwards transport commands to Music
 Assistant.
